    array.push(cH, "The dollar opened the week at a 19-month high, and Paris sent nothing new to answer it.|Sterling waits for Tuesday while the greenback starts Monday on the front foot.|Japan's economy stalled in the third quarter, and the yen lost a little more footing.|The franc had nothing to lean on overnight, and the dollar index sat at a 19-month high.|Oil slipped again at the open, giving the loonie one more worry before its CPI.|China's October numbers missed across the board, but the stand-off holds.|Weak Chinese demand is a small cloud over the kiwi's dairy story.|A quiet Asian night for two European currencies whose stories start later today.|The yen's side of this lean got weaker overnight.|Still dead level, with the franc's data due this morning.|China's soft data took a little shine off the Aussie, but not enough to matter.|Both sides start the week waiting: the euro on Paris, the kiwi on dairy.|Cheaper oil nudged this stand-off slightly toward the euro, on paper only.|The yen stumbled on GDP, but the pound has not shown up yet.|No fear in Asia, no help for the franc.|China's slowdown gives the pound a sliver of hope in this tie.|Level at +1 each, and Asia's data did not split them.|Oil gave the pound a small helping hand before Canada's inflation test.|Two Asian data misses, and they pulled in opposite directions.|The carry gap survived China's soft numbers.|China's slowdown hits both neighbours, so it does not separate them.|Oil dipped, China missed, and the lean barely noticed.|The yen blinked first, but the stand-off stays.|A calm Asian session keeps the kiwi's lean over the franc.|Oil gave way a little more, and the dairy side is still waiting for its auction.|Both legs got weaker overnight, so this lean is under watch.|Two weak currencies, and cheaper oil did the loonie no favours.|The yen's small edge over the franc wobbled on Japan's GDP.|Gold got no new fuel overnight, and the dollar stayed firm.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED~Dec 25bp hike priced 92–94%, 50bp tail down to 6–8% (from 11.5% Fri); no Fed policy shift overnight; Warsh 19:00 Bucharest.|CONFIRMED~No French spread or budget item overnight; Senate resumes the PLFSS spending debate today.|CONFIRMED~No BoE item overnight; UK jobs Tue 09:00 and CPI Wed 09:00 Bucharest.|WEAKENED (watch)~Q3 GDP −0.1% ann. vs +0.3% exp.: shadow R3 −1, raw −0.9 held at 0; BoJ Dec pricing fade not seen; no MoF comment.|CONFIRMED~No SNB item; Swiss Q3 GDP flash 10:00 Bucharest (after this check).|CONFIRMED (watch)~Brent −1% to $94.86 early Monday on IEA surplus view (N1 info only); Canada CPI 15:30, poll 3.2%.|CONFIRMED (watch)~China Oct data missed (IP 4.8%, retail 0.4%, FAI −8.1% YTD): MEDIUM, no factor; RBA minutes Tue 02:30.|CONFIRMED (watch)~China's soft retail sales are a dairy-demand risk; no RBNZ or vote update; GDT Tue 14:00.|CONFIRMED · fragile (gap −3)~Gold factor −3 unchanged; no ETF/central-bank data; 10y 5.14%; Bab el-Mandeb did not trigger risk-off.")
