    array.push(cH, "American shoppers kept spending where it counts, and the dollar side of this pair grew one notch.|Britain's jobs report gave the pound a cleaner headline, but America's shoppers gave the dollar more.|The dollar leg picked up fresh fuel while Tokyo only repeated its warning.|A firmer American consumer widened the distance between a hiking Fed and a 0% SNB.|Two weak spots for the loonie this week, and now a stronger greenback on the other side.|This stand-off just tipped: one dollar point is enough to give the pair a lean.|The kiwi waited for dairy news while the dollar collected a stronger data point.|A lower UK jobless rate leaned the right way for this pair, without moving a score yet.|Neither side got a decisive push today, so the thin lean toward the yen survives.|A tie with no new ammunition on either side.|The Aussie is still bruised from the minutes, but the euro never got its chance to close the gap.|Dairy day came and went without a verified number, so the kiwi keeps its small lead.|Two tired currencies, one quiet afternoon, still level.|Sterling got a jobs report it can argue about; the yen got another warning from Tokyo.|Better British jobless numbers keep this lean intact, with a small upside if they count as hawkish.|The pound's report could narrow this gap, but not enough to create a lean.|The tie-breakers arrived, but only one could be checked.|Two possible upgrades sit behind this pair's five-point lean.|The risk-mood pair heads into tonight's Nvidia results with a weakened Aussie leg.|Carry against zero yield held up through a data day that belonged to others.|The kiwi's dairy test is still unread, so the Tasman tie holds.|The loonie's soft inflation is still the stronger story in this commodity matchup.|A kiwi without a verified dairy number meets a yen with another verbal shield.|Nothing moved either leg, so the four-point lean rests where it was.|Dairy is unconfirmed, but the loonie's own weakness keeps this lean healthy.|The loonie's soft spot and the yen's verbal shield both stay in place.|A one-point gap between two weak currencies, unchanged by a quiet day.|Two former havens, and only the yen got even a verbal boost today.|The dollar got stronger in the shadow, but gold's own model did not move.")
    array.push(cC, "CONFIRMED (strengthened)~Retail sales +0.2% in line but control group +0.6% vs +0.4%; Musalem: several hikes by spring. Shadow R3 +2, raw 6.3 → +6.|CONFIRMED~No new OAT–Bund reading after 155.0bp (16 Nov); Senate PLFSS vote expected 18 Nov.|CONFIRMED (mixed data)~Jobless 4.6% vs 4.7% but payrolls −34k, pay slowing; Dec BoE odds 80–90%. +2 if scored hawkish.|CONFIRMED (watch)~Katayama repeats US coordination and readiness to act; shadow R3 −1, raw −0.9 held at 0.|CONFIRMED (watch)~No SNB item; VIX-25 trigger not confirmed by a verified close.|CONFIRMED (bearish reinforced)~No new Canadian item; CPI miss carried: shadow raw −4.5 held at −4.|WEAKENED (watch)~No verified Australian item since the morning; RBA 6–3 split still the latest signal; wages Wed 02:30.|CONFIRMED~GDT auction result not verified at check time; no RBNZ item.|CONFIRMED · fragile (gap −3)~Gold factor G −3 unchanged; XAU shadow = G + USD shadow = +3; no ETF or central-bank data.")
